    "content": "Figure 2:\nCaption: PBPK model structure for simulating PFOA/PFOS exposure during lactation in humans (maternal, left; infant, right). Maternal exposure is by direct intake; the infant exposure is through milk. No data were available for PFOA or PFOS partitioning into mammary tissue; chemical in plasma was assumed to be in direct contact with the milk compartment. Transfer from the plasma to the milk compartment was assumed to be flow-limited. Limited data was available for concentrations of PFAAs in the infant; thus, the infant was treated as a single compartment. Only the free fraction of chemical in plasma was available for uptake into tissues or milk.",
